254
00:16:25,770 --> 00:16:29,110
Oh, man. If I ever run into that guy again, you know what I'm gonna do?

255
00:16:29,270 --> 00:16:31,230
Bend over?

256
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:38,870
And then Zana just let one rip.

257
00:16:43,910 --> 00:16:47,460
Look, not that I don't enjoy talking about people who we went to high school with...

258
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:49,670
- ...because I do.     - Ha, ha.

259
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:52,170
But, um, maybe we can talk about something else.

260
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:54,720
Like you. I don't even know where you work.

261
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:57,300
- You know where I work.     - I do?

262
00:16:57,470 --> 00:17:00,390
The movie theater. You used to come in all the time.

263
00:17:01,430 --> 00:17:05,940
- You still work at the Multiplex?     - Like I'd give up that job. Ha, ha.

264
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:09,060
Free popcorn and candy any time I want?

265
00:17:09,230 --> 00:17:11,940
- I can get you free posters for your room.     - Thanks, I'm set.

266
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:15,570
Do you live with your parents?

267
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:17,950
Yeah, but I can stay out as late as I want.

268
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:26,370
Wow, they really got you guys. Your TV, the chairs.

269
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:29,290
Yeah, your microwave, the stereo.

270
00:17:29,460 --> 00:17:32,880
Oh, man, he took the five of spades.

271
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:35,550
Oh, no, no, here it is.

272
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:39,090
Oh, my God. What happened?

273
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:43,930
Oh. Um, Joey was born, and then 28 years later, I was robbed.

274
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:49,810
So how was your date?

275
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:53,400
Well, you know how I always wanted to go out with Chip in high school?

276
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:57,820
Well, tonight, I actually went out with Chip Matthews in high school.

277
00:17:58,610 --> 00:18:00,240
Oh, honey, I'm sorry.

278
00:18:00,410 --> 00:18:03,330
No, it's okay. Not only did I get to go out with Chip Matthews...

279
00:18:03,490 --> 00:18:05,290
...I got to dump Chip Matthews.

280
00:18:05,450 --> 00:18:08,330
- Oh, that's so great.     - I know.

281
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,130
- Hey.     - Hey.

282
00:18:11,290 --> 00:18:13,290
So, uh, what did the insurance company say?

283
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:14,500
Oh, they said, uh:

284
00:18:14,670 --> 00:18:18,010
"You don't have insurance here, so stop calling us."

285
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,800
You didn't tell her?

286
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:28,520
Okay, fine.

287
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:30,810
- Pheebs?     - Yeah. Hi.

288
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:34,110
Hi. Listen, uh...

289
00:18:34,570 --> 00:18:37,650
...this cat belongs to a little girl.

290
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:41,110
All right? There are flyers all over the place.

291
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:43,490
I'm sorry, sweetie.

292
00:18:44,030 --> 00:18:46,740
Hey, we can take her back with you if you want.

293
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:50,580
Oh. Mm-hm.

294
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:54,250
But, you know, she chose to find me.

295
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:56,750
I mean, I have to respect her decision, right?

296
00:18:58,550 --> 00:19:01,050
- That's a good call.     - That's right.

297
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:03,800
No, no. Hey, enough is enough.

298
00:19:03,970 --> 00:19:06,390
Look, I'm sorry that you feel guilty or whatever...

299
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:10,100
...about spending time with your new mom. But this is not your old mom.

300
00:19:10,270 --> 00:19:11,770
This is a cat. Okay?

301
00:19:11,940 --> 00:19:14,560
Julio the cat.

302
00:19:14,730 --> 00:19:16,610
Not Mom. Cat.

303
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:24,570
It's okay.

304
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:28,240
Ross, how many parents have you lost?

305
00:19:29,410 --> 00:19:30,750
None.

306
00:19:30,910 --> 00:19:34,630
Okay, then you don't know what it feels like when one of them comes back. Do you?

307
00:19:39,130 --> 00:19:41,420
I believe this is my mother.

308
00:19:41,590 --> 00:19:43,930
Even if I'm wrong, who cares?

309
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:47,560
Just be a friend, okay? Be supportive.

310
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:52,140
I'm sorry.

311
00:19:53,270 --> 00:19:54,730
Okay.

312
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:58,400
I don't know what to say. Heh.

313
00:20:01,150 --> 00:20:05,110
You could say you're sorry to her mom.

314
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:13,920
I think she would like that.

315
00:20:24,970 --> 00:20:27,720
Come here. Here, come here, come here.

316
00:20:29,890 --> 00:20:31,680
Mrs. Buffay?

317
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,310
Sorry about what I said.

318
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:40,780
Um, it was insensitive of me to say...

319
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:43,280
...that you were just a cat.

320
00:20:45,530 --> 00:20:50,830
When, clearly, you are also the reincarnated spirit...

321
00:20:51,370 --> 00:20:52,450
...of my friend's mother.

322
00:20:55,540 --> 00:20:57,080
Thank you.

323
00:20:57,750 --> 00:20:59,750
- We both forgive you.     - Heh.

324
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:03,420
What are you gonna do about the little girl?

325
00:21:03,590 --> 00:21:06,340
Yeah. Okay, listen.

326
00:21:06,510 --> 00:21:10,850
Um, Mom, I hope you know that you still mean a lot to me.

327
00:21:11,010 --> 00:21:13,600
And you're welcome to come back any time.

328
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:15,480
Pheebs?

329
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:19,230
If she could come back as a couch, we'd really appreciate it.

330
00:21:21,110 --> 00:21:22,780
Come on, Mom, I'm gonna take you home.

331
00:21:22,940 --> 00:21:25,110
- I'll go with you.     - Me too.

332
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:29,070
Oh, uh, you know, I got an extra futon.

333
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:33,160
Dude, you don't have to brag. We got nothing here.

334
00:21:37,210 --> 00:21:39,070

